From 78e50c37948ace330a44d2874787fa10e64b8bec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bob <robertramsay78@googlemail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:16:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Animate: 8-direction movement layout and a Test mode;
 clearing frames really clears

8 directions (anim_dirs): each actor can have an animation for N NE E SE S
SW W NW instead of Walk, laid out as a compass round Idle on the Animate
page. Empty directions borrow from the others (turned round when 'Turn to
face left' is on), and an empty Idle stands facing the way it last moved.
Once mode holds the last frame - a ship veering and holding its lean.

Engine: A_AMODE bit 0 = 8 directions, table of 12 entries, the direction is
taken from each frame's move (dir_tab), v_dir remembers the last one, mode 3
= stand facing. Checked in FS-UAE with an arrow per direction.

Test: drives the preview with the arrow keys, WASD or a gamepad and picks
the animation as the Amiga will.

Fix: the first change on the Animate page now switches the old two-frame
animation off, so clearing every frame no longer falls back to it (it kept
flashing between two frames).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BQFSzGarhTTpK2DHf8XzFr
